DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kometa Fellows 2026: Field Journalism\, Photography\, and
  Writing
DESCRIPTION:Kometa\, a French literary and journalism magazine\, awards fel
 lowships to journalists\, writers\, and photographers documenting reality 
 in contexts of war\, censorship\, or severe social and political tensions.
  Projects must be rooted in direct field experience and focused on contemp
 orary rather than historical events. Projects already under a contractual 
 agreement are ineligible. AMOUNT: €10\,000 per Fellow\, six Fellows sele
 cted. WHAT FELLOWS RECEIVE: one year of funding\; publication of the compl
 eted project (partial or full) in Kometa\; opportunity to contribute to th
 e monthly newsletter\; mentorship through editorial collaboration. 2026 FO
 CUS AREAS: disinformation and narrative wars\; political and social change
 s in the Gulf. DEADLINE: 31 July 2026. APPLY via the Tally form (https://t
 ally.so/r/J9XxMK)\, in French or English (about 30 to 45 minutes). Contact
 : fellows@kometarevue.com.\n\nOrganisation: Kometa (French literary and jo
 urnalism magazine)\nLocation: Remote / field-based (international)\nAward:
  €10\,000 per Fellow\, six Fellows selected. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: One year of funding for field work and research\n\nMore: https://komet
 arevue.com/page/fellows?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://kometarevue.com/page/fellows?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / field-based (international)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bow-seat-true-blue-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T221230Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: True Blue Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Bow Seat's True Blue Fellowship funds youth-led projects that u
 se the creative arts as their primary method for building awareness or dri
 ving action on ocean\, waterways and climate change issues\, including env
 ironmental justice. Twelve fellows are selected each year and receive up t
 o USD 2\,500 in project funding alongside mentorship\, capacity-building p
 rogramming\, and access to a peer community that includes the Future Blue 
 Youth Council and Bow Seat staff. ELIGIBILITY: youth worldwide aged 16 to 
 24 at the start of the fellowship period in January. Individuals\, groups 
 and youth-led organisations may apply\, with one designated project leader
  for a group. Projects must be new or emerging\, meaning less than two yea
 rs old\, and should span at least one year running January to December. Ap
 plications must be submitted in English\, though translation tools are acc
 eptable\, and applicants should be comfortable with spoken English for pee
 r collaboration. NOTE: this is a youth programme with an upper age limit o
 f 24\, and the creative-arts requirement is central rather than incidental
 \, so proposals built on other methods are out of scope. Deadline 30 Augus
 t 2026 at 11:59pm ET.\n\nOrganisation: Bow Seat Ocean Awareness Programs\n
 Location: Remote\, open to youth worldwide.\nAward: Up to USD 2\,500 in pr
 oject funding per fellow\, plus mentorship and capacity-building programmi
 ng. Twelve youth are selected annually. No application fee.\nDuration: One
  year\, January to December 2027\n\nMore: https://bowseat.org/programs/tru
 e-blue-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://bowseat.org/programs/true-blue-fellowship/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, open to youth worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mycelia-fellowship-social-resonance-lab-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260921T221230Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mycelia Fellowship 2026 (Social Resonance Lab)
DESCRIPTION:The inaugural Mycelia Fellowship by Social Resonance Lab\, a co
 llaborative research studio exploring how ethical storytelling fosters hum
 an connection\, selects two practitioners advancing innovative projects at
  the intersection of ethical storytelling\, arts\, civic engagement\, AI\,
  or the digital landscape. TWO TRACKS: Arts as a Civic Tool (artistic prac
 tice for public engagement and social issues) and AI and the Digital Lands
 cape (technology's influence on narratives and collective memory). Fellows
  receive a USD 2\,000 stipend\, direct advising and consultancy from the S
 RL team\, a published piece on the SRL Substack\, a guest spot on an upcom
 ing ethical storytelling podcast\, and co-lead a workshop presenting their
  work to practitioners and the public. The fellowship strengthens\, docume
 nts\, refines or scales EXISTING projects\; do not pitch a completely new 
 idea\, and connect your work clearly to ethical storytelling and one of th
 e two tracks. ELIGIBILITY: US residents only (including territories\, must
  be able to file a W-9 and use a US bank account) with an existing project
  underway\, intersectional practice awareness\, and strong writing and res
 earch skills. Remote\, 8 weeks\, November to December 2026. No application
  fee. Deadline: 13 September 2026\, 11:59 PM.\n\nOrganisation: Social Reso
 nance Lab\nLocation: Remote\, US residents only (including territories)\nA
 ward: USD 2\,000 stipend per fellow\; two fellows selected for the inaugur
 al cohort\nDuration: 8-week remote fellowship\, 1 November to 31 December 
 2026\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdj_qxRZmRZcNdVcQvX
 z9mZIhZTj-Iau-cZVb-kowZtRER6Dw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdj_qxRZmRZcNdVcQvXz9mZIhZTj-I
 au-cZVb-kowZtRER6Dw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, US residents only (including territories)
END:VEVENT
